   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law and a chapter of the laws\nof 2023 amending the environmental conservation law relating to a Long Island\ndeer management pilot program, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n4804-A and A. 5542-A, in relation to an urban deer management pilot program",
    "basePrintNo": "S8052",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8052-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Ren §11-0522 to be §11-0522-a, amd §§11-0522-a, 11-0505, 11-0901 & 11-0931, En Con L; amd §5, Chap of 2023 (as proposed in S.4804-A & A.5542-A)",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8052\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law and a chapter of the\nlaws of 2023 amending the environmental conservation law relating to a\nLong Island deer management pilot program, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S. 4804-A and A. 5542-A, in relation to an urban deer\nmanagement pilot program\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of chapter\n704 of the laws of 2023 to refine the regulatory structure laid out in\nthat chapter.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 makes technical changes, clarifies and augments the require-\nments for nuisance wildlife specialists, and refines permit require-\nments.\n\nSections 2, 3, and 4 make technical updates.\n\nSection 5 simplifies the study required to be completed by the Depart-\nment of Environmental Conservation (DEC).\n\nSection 6 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter to\nclarify and augment the requirements for nuisance wildlife specialists,\nrefine permit requirements, and simplify the study to be conducted by\nDEC.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to Chapter 704 of the Laws of 2023. Both\nS.4804A and A.5542A passed the Senate and Assembly, respectively, in\nJune 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMay reduce costs to the state as compared to the underlying chapter by\nlimiting matters DEC will be required to study.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nOn the same date and in the same manner as the underlying chapter.\n",
